.sp
.LP
\fISolaris Modular Debugger Guide\fR
.SH WARNINGS
.sp
.LP
When \fBlibumem\fR aborts the process using \fBabort\fR(3C), any existing
signal handler for \fBSIGABRT\fR is called. If the signal handler performs
allocations, undefined behavior can result.
.SH NOTES
.sp
.LP
Some of the debugging features work only for allocations smaller than 16
kilobytes in size. Allocations larger than 16 kilobytes could have reduced
support.
.sp
.LP
Activating any of the library's debugging features could significantly increase
the library's memory footprint and decrease its performance.
.SS "Debug Mode Reference"
.sp
.LP
The following table summarizes the debug modes and their corresponding internal
flags:
.sp
.TS
box;
cb | cb | cb | cb
l | l | l | l .
Debug Option	Flag(s)	Detects	Overhead
_
audit	UMF_AUDIT	Memory leaks, allocation history	30-50%
deadbeef	UMF_DEADBEEF	Use-after-free, uninitialized data	10-15%
redzone	UMF_REDZONE	Buffer overruns	5-10%
contents	UMF_CONTENTS	Buffer corruption (with audit)	10-15%
guards	UMF_DEADBEEF | UMF_REDZONE	All of above	10-20%
lite	UMF_LITE	Same as guards, lightweight	15-25%
default	All of above	Comprehensive debugging	50-70%
.TE
.sp
.LP
Debug flags can be combined. Some flags automatically enable others:
.RS +4
.TP
.ie t \(bu
.el o
\fBaudit\fR automatically enables \fBguards\fR (deadbeef + redzone)
.RE
.RS +4
.TP
.ie t \(bu
.el o
\fBcontents\fR requires \fBaudit\fR to be effective
.RE
.RS +4
.TP
.ie t \(bu
.el o
\fBdefault\fR enables \fBaudit\fR, \fBcontents\fR, and \fBguards\fR
.RE
.RS +4
.TP
.ie t \(bu
.el o
\fBlite\fR is mutually exclusive with \fBaudit\fR (lite is used when audit
would be too expensive)
.RE
.sp
.LP
\fBCommon Debugging Workflows:\fR
.sp
To detect memory leaks:
.sp
.in +2
.nf
UMEM_DEBUG=audit UMEM_LOGGING=transaction=10M ./myapp
# Inspect with the umem(1) tool, no debugger required:
umem --pid $! findleaks
umem --pid $! status
# Or attach a debugger:
(gdb) source /path/to/tools/gdb/umem_gdb.py
(gdb) umem findleaks
(gdb) umem status
.fi
.in -2
.sp
To detect buffer overruns:
.sp
.in +2
.nf
UMEM_DEBUG=guards ./myapp
# Program aborts with diagnostic if overrun detected
.fi
.in -2
.sp
To track use-after-free:
.sp
.in +2
.nf
UMEM_DEBUG=guards ./myapp
# Freed buffers filled with 0xdeadbeef
# Program aborts if pattern corrupted on next allocation
.fi
.in -2
.sp
To analyze buffer corruption:
.sp
.in +2
.nf
UMEM_DEBUG=audit,contents=1024 \\
UMEM_LOGGING=transaction=10M,contents=50M \\
./myapp
# Contents log saves buffer state at free time
.fi
.in -2
.sp
For production debugging with minimal overhead:
.sp
.in +2
.nf
UMEM_DEBUG=guards ./myapp
# Only 10-20% overhead, catches most common bugs
.fi
.in -2
.SS "Debug Mode Interactions"
.sp
.LP
When multiple debug options are enabled, they interact as follows:
.RS +4
.TP
.ie t \(bu
.el o
Setting \fBUMEM_DEBUG\fR automatically disables Per-Thread Caching (PTC) to
ensure all allocations pass through the debug infrastructure
.RE
.RS +4
.TP
.ie t \(bu
.el o
Caches created with \fBUMC_NODEBUG\fR flag bypass all debugging features for
that cache only
.RE
.RS +4
.TP
.ie t \(bu
.el o
The \fBUMC_NOTOUCH\fR flag prevents pattern fills (deadbeef) but allows other
debug features like auditing
.RE
.RS +4
.TP
.ie t \(bu
.el o
Large allocations (>16KB) may not support all debug features
.RE
.RS +4
.TP
.ie t \(bu
.el o
Debug features work for both \fBumem_alloc\fR(3MALLOC) and
\fBumem_cache_alloc\fR(3MALLOC)
.RE
.SS "Debugger Extensions"
.sp
.LP
The \fBlibumem\fR library includes debugger extensions for both
\fBgdb\fR(1) and \fBlldb\fR(1):
.sp
.ne 2
.na
\fBGDB Extension\fR
.ad
.RS 16n
Load the extension with:
.sp
.in +2
.nf
(gdb) source /path/to/umem_gdb.py
.fi
.in -2
.sp
Available commands:
.RS +4
.TP
.ie t \(bu
.el o
\fBumem findleaks\fR \- group allocated buffers by stack
.RE
.RS +4
.TP
.ie t \(bu
.el o
\fBumem log\fR \- chronological transaction log
.RE
.RS +4
.TP
.ie t \(bu
.el o
\fBumem status\fR \- per-cache statistics
.RE
.RS +4
.TP
.ie t \(bu
.el o
\fBumem walk\fR \- stream allocated / freed / log entries
.RE
.RS +4
.TP
.ie t \(bu
.el o
\fBumem whatis\fR \- identify which cache owns an address
.RE
.RS +4
.TP
.ie t \(bu
.el o
\fBumem bufctl\fR \- pretty-print the bufctl audit record
.RE
.RS +4
.TP
.ie t \(bu
.el o
\fBumem snapshot\fR \- write binary or text snapshot for offline analysis
.RE
.RS +4
.TP
.ie t \(bu
.el o
\fBumem break\fR \- conditional breakpoints on alloc / free / error events
.RE
.RS +4
.TP
.ie t \(bu
.el o
\fBumem help\fR \- show all commands
.RE
.RE
.sp
.ne 2
.na
\fBLLDB Extension\fR
.ad
.RS 16n
Load the extension with:
.sp
.in +2
.nf
(lldb) command script import /path/to/umem_lldb.py
.fi
.in -2
.sp
Same commands as GDB extension.
.RE
.sp
.LP
These extensions provide runtime inspection of umem state. For detailed
allocation information including stack traces, use with \fBUMEM_DEBUG=audit\fR.
For complete documentation, see \fBumem_inspect\fR(3),
\fBumem_debugging\fR(7), and \fBtools/DEBUGGING.md\fR in the source tree.
.SS "Performance Impact"
.sp
.LP
Debug features have the following performance characteristics:
.RS +4
.TP
.ie t \(bu
.el o
\fBguards\fR: 10-20% overhead (pattern fill/check on alloc/free)
.RE
.RS +4
.TP
.ie t \(bu
.el o
\fBaudit\fR: 30-50% overhead (stack unwinding on every alloc/free)
.RE
.RS +4
.TP
.ie t \(bu
.el o
\fBUMEM_LOGGING\fR: 40-60% overhead (logging transaction history)
.RE
.RS +4
.TP
.ie t \(bu
.el o
Combined \fBdefault\fR mode: 50-70% overhead
.RE
.sp
.LP
Memory overhead varies but typically adds 100-500 bytes per allocation for
audit structures and redzone guards.
.sp
.LP
Note: Setting \fBUMEM_DEBUG\fR automatically disables Per-Thread Caching (PTC)
to ensure all allocations pass through the debug infrastructure.
.SS "Common Debugging Workflows"
.sp
.LP
To detect memory leaks:
.sp
.in +2
.nf
UMEM_DEBUG=audit ./myapp
# Either use the umem(1) tool against the running process:
umem --pid $(pgrep myapp) findleaks
# Or attach a debugger:
(gdb) source /path/to/tools/gdb/umem_gdb.py
(gdb) umem findleaks
(gdb) umem status
.fi
.in -2
.sp
.LP
To detect buffer overruns:
.sp
.in +2
.nf
UMEM_DEBUG=guards ./myapp
# Program will abort with detailed error if overrun detected
.fi
.in -2
.sp
.LP
To track use-after-free:
.sp
.in +2
.nf
UMEM_DEBUG=guards ./myapp
# Freed buffers filled with 0xdeadbeef pattern
# Program aborts if pattern corrupted on next allocation
.fi
.in -2
